Dataset rlp_influencers_dataset {
  label: 'RLP Influencer Directory (CF-13963)'
  description: '''
    The influencer lookup, deliberately separated from rlp_sales_dataset.

    Only rlp_dim_influencers is in here, so the `is_my_role is true` rule has nothing to propagate to:
    - h_role = admin   -> influencer 1 only
    - h_role = analyst -> influencer 2 only
    - h_role = viewer  -> influencer 3 only

    Putting this same rule in rlp_sales_dataset is what breaks the OR: it propagates dim -> fact and drops
    sale 2 (admin destination / analyst influencer). One dataset cannot both keep sale 2 and hide influencer 2,
    because sale 2 IS influencer 2's row. Splitting the datasets is what makes both requirements satisfiable.
  '''
  data_source_name: 'demodb'

  models: [
    rlp_dim_influencers,
  ]
  relationships: []

  permission influencer_role_access {
    field: r(rlp_dim_influencers.is_my_role)
    operator: 'is'
    value: true
  }

  view {
    model rlp_dim_influencers {}
  }
}
